-- title:
--   Vertical Line Point At Append Point
-- statement:
--   **The vertical line through a point evaluates to the appended point.**
--
--   Let $u\in\mathbb{F}_q^m$ and $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$. The axis-parallel line in the new coordinate direction, based at the point obtained by appending zero to $u$, has parametrization
--
--   $$
--   \ell(t)=(u,t).
--   $$
--
--   Therefore its value at $x$ is
--
--   $$
--   \ell(x)=(u,x).
--   $$
--
--   This coordinate identity identifies vertical-line evaluation in the successor space with evaluation at the corresponding appended point. It is used when converting vertical-line estimates into point-measurement estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.verticalLine_pointAt_appendPoint`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
